  "about": "Chapter one's hidden map. The player only sees the room they're in and its exits. threat = the fight in the room; enemy = who holds it (regular rooms only; elites and bosses come from their threat) (elites on 5/15/25, bosses on 10/20/30). goal = one of the chapter's three hidden goals, found by looking. requires 'goals' = sealed until all three are found. Keep room text to about two sentences. arena = the fight's board, drawn as text rows: '.' deck, '~' open water, '#' crates, 'd' drums, 'n' nets, 'p' pumps, '?' a loose crate (there half the time), 'f' fuel fire, 'c' live cable, 'b' chemical bilge, 'h' split decking, 'P' your start, 'E' enemy starts (first is the lead).",
